    description: "Pass 18 finding IIIIIII. Distribution of access_mode presence across 108649 edges by edge.type: calls 41412/60831 (68.1%); event_publishes 103/103 (100%); instantiates 5567/7803 (71.3%); module_attr_ref 556/1326 (41.9%); references 2520/4250 (59.3%); contains 0/22529; decorated_by 0/403; depends_on 0/6; depends_on_manifest 0/26; dispatches_to 0/617; extends 0/147; implements 0/6; imports 0/10480; inherits 0/1; overrides 0/1; script_src 0/1; uses 0/119. 12 of 17 edge types have 0 coverage; 5 have partial coverage (none 100% except event_publishes). Whether the absence means 'not applicable' or 'not yet implemented' is undocumented. Consumer querying access_mode needs to know whether to interpret None as 'irrelevant' or 'missing data'."  # 30e3
    fields:  # 30e3
      statement: "When a meta field is selectively populated across edge types, the schema should document which edge types carry the field and which don't. access_mode is unpopulated for 12 of 17 edge.type values without any explicit schema declaration of which types are in scope."  # 30e3
      root_cause: "access_mode population is wired in 5 edge-emission paths (calls 68%, instantiates 71%, references 59%, module_attr_ref 42%, event_publishes 100%) and the other 12 edge types never set the field. There is no declared policy that distinguishes 'access_mode applies' vs 'not applicable' edge types."  # 30e3
